{
  "dom_id": "step-q213190",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph representing the relation $R=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y={x}^{2}\\}?$",
  "worked_solution": "A binary relation can be visualized using a plot (or graph), where \n\n- the first set goes along the horizontal line,\n\n- the second set goes along the vertical line,\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines a point with coordinates $(x,y)$ on the plot.\n\nIn our case, the plot contains all the points in ${R}^{2}$ for which \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThese are the points that *lie* on the parabola $y={x}^{2}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14267734/assets/a6fa67f5d665d40b7d05efc95ae5ecdc1a1b91614fcd13d69ed147cca46e16b0.png)",
